  reason: "The verb's leaf producer is host Rust because its subject is a filesystem walk the hermetic floor refuses; the route around that leaf is hand-mirrored because none of the three modeled modules is in the v1 seed's emitted closure, and the two alternatives are worse -- routing through the interpreter makes it load-bearing for a NEW capability while two lanes delete it, and growing the emitter's closure to reach extdeps.bazel.label is a larger seed change than the verb it serves. What the growth buys is that the repository's instruments become addressable by label at all: before it, no target in this repository could be run by name. The diagnostic-census producer and its cli_run carriers joined under the same reasoning: the whole-tree compile-clean closure is a host effect no hermetic witness may run, and the census restores the reachability the gunbc#9160 sweep removed with the unrostered bin. The 2026-09-09 raw-census rework added the identity, disposition, refusal and specimen carriers: binding the observation to its source vector, compiler, policy, schema and closure is hashing and a total-match specimen over CompilerDiagnostic, both host facts. The 2026-09-20 pattern admission added the parse_target_pattern mirror (TargetPattern, TargetPatternRefusal, target_pattern_refusal_text, parse_pattern_package) beside the parse_label mirror it delegates the single-target form to, plus test_operand_set_form_refusal_rendered: a SET form is admitted by the grammar and REFUSED by the route with status 2 (operator ruling 2026-09-21), because its only admissible executor is the native test route and no interpreter delegation may stand in for it -- so that growth was the admission mirror and one refusal text, and no selection or execution semantics. In the same change the host's OperandNotALabel refusal arm and label_refusal_rendered deleted as unconstructible: every label refusal now arrives inside PatternLabelRefused. THAT SCOPE SENTENCE NO LONGER DESCRIBES THIS SEAM, AND IT IS CORRECTED HERE RATHER THAN LEFT STANDING (v2 foundation package 9). The native test route is now reachable by operand, and both of the things the old sentence excluded are present: SELECTION -- target_pattern_within with target_pattern_package, package_within and render_target_pattern, the mirror of the containment that decides WHICH executor answers an operand, plus native_route_default_pattern, which holds NO spelling of the native universe: it parses NATIVE_ROUTE_DEFAULT_PATTERN, the constant gunbc.native_route_seed_boundary_emit renders from the one declaration into native_route_seed_boundary_generated.rs under the generated-artifact drift wall, while the lane runner passes the emitted compiler no default at all (the compiler adjudicates by its own; the seed passes a pattern only when the operator wrote one). The claim route's universe is the part of this selection that is STILL a hand mirror -- claim_route_universe mirrors gunbc.discovery_census claim_route_universe, disclosed beside the recurring-failure-mode row test_identity_restated_as_a_location_predicate_beside_the_marker and not projected by this change; and EXECUTION SEMANTICS -- run_native_test_route, which spawns the emitted compiler over the operand's pattern and partitions its answer, with native_lane_runner's NativeRouteOutcome, NativeRunAdmission and run_required_v2_native_inner carrying that partition as a typed value so no consumer recovers it from rendered text. This is the first execution semantics on this seam and it is counted as such: DESIGN section 7 asks for a declared row that is COUNTABLE, and a row whose reason excludes what the file now holds is worse than an uncounted declaration, because it tells a reader the seed is smaller than it is. THE MIGRATION TRIGGER IS UNCHANGED BY THIS GROWTH and is the same one the route has always waited on: these mirrors dissolve when the modeled modules enter an emitted closure, at which point the route is the .dag fold and this file is deleted rather than trimmed. A LATER GROWTH ADDED THE MEMBER-SCOPED STANDING and is counted here too: NativeMemberVerdict and NativeMemberTermination mirror v2.compiler.native_test_vocabulary NativeTestVerdict at its discriminant and v2.workflow.native_route_member_termination native_route_member_termination's result, native_member_termination mirrors that fold ARM FOR ARM INCLUDING ITS PRECEDENCE, and native_member_outcome maps the result onto this verb's termination. That growth is NOT a new authority -- the fold is modeled and its precedence is argued in the .dag source -- BUT ITS PARITY WITH THE MODEL IS UNCHECKED, AND AN EARLIER VERSION OF THIS SENTENCE CLAIMED OTHERWISE (review 70196). It said the mirror carries a discriminating red so that drift from the model is detectable. That is rung inflation of exactly the kind DESIGN section 4b(1) names, and it contradicted this row's own standing sentence two paragraphs above: what is NOT claimed is that the mirror is checked, only that it is enumerated. WHAT THE TWO TESTS ACTUALLY DO: the Rust test the_precedence_matches_the_modeled_fold compares native_member_termination against literals hard-coded in Rust, and the .dag witnesses compare native_route_member_termination against literals authored in .dag. NOTHING COMPARES THE TWO. Change the precedence in the model and update its .dag witness to match, and both suites stay green while the host answers differently -- the Rust test catches a Rust-side edit, which is the mirror drifting from its own test rather than from its model. AND THAT TEST DOES NOT RUN ON THE MERGE PATH AT ALL: cargo test -p v1-compiler --lib is executed by no CI step, which is the declared drop gunbc.rung_drop rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path. So this growth sits at the SAME mitigatable rung as the rest of this row and for the same reason, and its parity is carried by review diligence. WHAT WOULD CLIMB IT is a parity check that runs the same discriminating cases through BOTH folds and compares the results -- which needs the model executed from the host, and would additionally need a CI step that runs it before it establishes anything. It dissolves on the SAME trigger as the rest of this row. THE 2026-10-02 FRESHNESS GROWTH (gunbc#13007) added the binary-freshness mirror: BinaryInput, BinaryInputObservation, BinaryFreshness, binary_built_elsewhere, binary_freshness_step, assess_binary_freshness and binary_freshness_rendered mirror gunbc.target_invocation arm for arm, and dep_info_inputs, classify_binary_inputs, build_start_anchor, observe_binary_inputs_of, observe_binary_inputs, test_verb_checked and test_verb_after are the effectful half -- reading the running binary's cargo dep-info, its fingerprint unit's build-start stamp, and each input's mtime, which no .dag fold can do. Its parity with the model is unchecked in exactly the sense stated above for the member fold, and it dissolves on the same trigger.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Discharge each declaration when its modeled realization is emitted rather than authored. The target_invocation_host subset deletes when gunbc.target_invocation and gunbc.instrument_targets enter the emitted closure of whatever renders gunbc's CLI; the behavioral_receipt_host subset deletes when the three already-modeled behavioral producers gain emitted native realization. A PARTIAL migration is admissible and expected: label admission dissolves when extdeps.bazel.label is emitted, independently of either producer family. Moving a declaration to another host file or adding a parity witness does not discharge it -- both leave the hand-authored declaration standing.",
